+# US-07: Set hyperparameters
+
+| | |
+| --- | --- |
+| Epic | WBMME-2 Model Training & Selection |
+| Requirement | MLE-F-008 |
+| Points / sprint | 5 / Sprint 1 |
+| Owner | Varnika (Member 2) |
+| SAD component | Model Selection & Training |
+| Design reference | DS-Model-02 |
+
+**Story.** As a Data Scientist I want to edit a model's hyperparameters, and be told clearly when a value is not allowed, so that I can tune a model without breaking it.
+
+## Acceptance criteria (SRS MLE-F-008, TC-MODEL-01 step 3)
+
+- [x] At least two hyperparameters per model are editable (every catalogue model has two).
+- [x] A value outside its range, of the wrong type, or for an unknown setting is refused before training starts.
+- [x] The message names the parameter and its permitted range, for example `C must be a number between 0.01 and 100.`
+- [x] Boundary values are accepted (for example C = 0.01 and C = 100) and values just outside are refused (0.009 and 100.01).
+- [x] Settings left out take the catalogue default.
+- [x] All problems are reported together, not one at a time.
+
+## Files
+
+| File | Purpose |
+| --- | --- |
+| `training/params.py` | `validate_params(model_key, raw)` returning clean params and a list of `ParamError` |
+| `training/views.py`, `urls.py` | `POST /api/models/<key>/params/validate` |
+| `training/tests/test_params.py`, `test_api_params.py` | Boundary-value and API tests, tagged `req("MLE-F-008")` |
+
+## API
+
+```
+POST /api/models/logistic_regression/params/validate
+{"params": {"C": -5}}
+
+400 {"error": "invalid_params", "message": "Some settings are outside their permitted range.",
+     "details": [{"field": "params.C", "message": "C must be a number between 0.01 and 100."}]}
+```
+
+`POST /api/train` (US-08) calls the same `validate_params`, so the check cannot be bypassed.
